From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:01:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: the PlayStation 4 platform, with the ps4-homebrew-dev
 SDK

A build for the PS4 (Orbis OS, which runs a FreeBSD 9 kernel) with the
ps4-homebrew-dev SDK, whose CMake toolchain sets PS4: a static library,
with libkernel and libSceLibcInternal as its libc, libm and pthreads, and
dlopen() from the SDK's libc. __ORBIS__ gives __PS4__ (__FREEBSD__ stays
defined), SDL_GetPlatform() is "PS4", and the dynamic API is off.

src/core/ps4 has what the PS4 drivers share: initializing libSceUserService
and libScePad once, and loading the system libraries the SDK has no link
stubs for (audio out, the keyboard, the IME dialog) with libSceSysmodule
and dlopen(), as the SDK's crt loads the ones a program links. SDL links
libScePad, libSceUserService, libSceSystemService, libSceSysmodule and
libSceAppContent.

- SDL2main: main() sets the XDG base directories that are not set, in
  /temp0 (the title's temporary data, which only a game application has)
  when libSceAppContent can mount it, otherwise in common_temp, which all
  homebrew shares; /data is not always mounted. When the program exits,
  it goes back to the home screen (sceSystemServiceLoadExec("exit")).
- Filesystem: the base path is the program's folder, from argv[0], or a
  package's /app0/; the preference path is in $XDG_DATA_HOME (or
  $HOME/.local/share), which SDL2main sets.
- Locale: the system language (sceSystemServiceParamGetInt()).
- Misc: SDL_OpenURL() opens the web browser.
- Timers are the Unix ones, on clock_gettime().

